  "summary_en": "A practitioners' guide to responsible AI in Ghana, published by Heritors Labs and GIZ FAIR Forward. It sets ethical principles, surveys existing Ghanaian laws, and recommends a national AI law and an AI Commission. It also covers development, sectors, skills and startups. Robotics and drones appear only in passing.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Ghana has no dedicated AI law; existing data protection, cybersecurity, e-transactions and IP laws apply",
   "Recommends enacting a comprehensive National AI Regulation Act with risk classification and impact assessments",
   "Recommends an independent National AI Commission created by an Act of Parliament",
   "Ethical principles: fairness, transparency, accountability and human oversight, privacy, human-centric design, sustainability and inclusion",
   "Notes pending Emerging Technologies Bill and National AI Strategy expected by December 2025"
